{"type":"flow-report","report":{"flowRunId":"01a0513c-6ca4-7361-83eb-e79187d77272","flowName":"spec-build","scriptHash":"sha256:d6d16c1866fda90f68a5a3fec68b1f5a3e656d5e635d8d21ba273208ba1b88d1","ordinalKeys":["flow:01a0513c-6ca4-7361-83eb-e79187d77272:k:spec-build:v1:sweep::sweep","flow:01a0513c-6ca4-7361-83eb-e79187d77272:k:spec-build:v1:reconcile::reconcile","flow:01a0513c-6ca4-7361-83eb-e79187d77272:k:spec-build:v1:publish:cp-build:publish-main-cp-build"],"observationOrder":[7953,7954,7955],"finalValue":{"campaign":"flashnext","repository":"mecattaf/flashnext","issue":{"number":"1","url":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json"},"worklist":{"path":"silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json","revision":"94809584466a5700025ea9bcf408994d2b380983","sha256":"sha256:d82210748f7034f64b1b43cd6bc45335a56b8449998229249233645d6a8b243d"},"state":"blocked","reconciled":{"merged":[{"mergeCommit":"ff1731c6c5886748faa13231e2f6012936bfb5dd","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/container-recipe-6e8621b55de3a3a9","revision":"sha256:6e8621b55de3a3a9c646edd59fb1c26372db042e230f9d2d3ec5a4e08d329361","taskId":"container-recipe"},{"mergeCommit":"1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/instruments-16ab40e19244fd0f","revision":"sha256:16ab40e19244fd0f9cde08858a2c348ff99e701e0a8ce46b6e99fc84b6d36c5b","taskId":"instruments"},{"mergeCommit":"754e1118d0ce0414aa2f72fb2a7fdaa668e857cc","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/host-tooling-ab66c582012f053f","revision":"sha256:ab66c582012f053ffa092301faf6a9b042d52ad26c6baa1b6d149083241af99d","taskId":"host-tooling"},{"mergeCommit":"d618da613f55c39f5c520dcd2f499bb07e8da225","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/bench-harness-3a8882e61c9b2ce9","revision":"sha256:3a8882e61c9b2ce9ef7a7904e06778f0284df952e4a68deb4f8e6e1caba1a225","taskId":"bench-harness"},{"mergeCommit":"bfd358b923b35a4a80dad2163d7e8ec16aaf81b6","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/morning-ledger-27a15022aaf7c70c","revision":"sha256:27a15022aaf7c70c3c32d63b27cf07bf64e1e0097b435707dd270c06ab414996","taskId":"morning-ledger"},{"mergeCommit":"377ba269689b458c10903c86e579816d39478b34","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/catalog-handoff-7f3033dbd7a5c6b6","revision":"sha256:7f3033dbd7a5c6b695b70874814d89053eec1372194895793dc8534f9f4d03ed","taskId":"catalog-handoff"},{"mergeCommit":"0a89657f40b8654fed9a050b77458f46f0e5c559","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/rdma-package-fe9122567f61a3ff","revision":"sha256:fe9122567f61a3ff2f0fa2ba872e08f885158cdaa3d584270bd72b3302f22bbc","taskId":"rdma-package"},{"mergeCommit":"bdc42fc2d0a44bc934845e3aa65421ba51b94721","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/usb4stream-bench-75b32ae929f161f9","revision":"sha256:75b32ae929f161f972eb9544f33d653ee19a939a595012f6c112e3c4e69bb00e","taskId":"usb4stream-bench"}],"checkpoints":[{"ref":"refs/tally/spec-build/v1/9580b7cc868de0369023d414/checkpoint/cp-build-d82210748f7034f64b1b43cd6bc45335a56b8449998229249233645d6a8b243d/1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304","revision":"1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304","taskId":"cp-build"}],"remaining":["proxy-tooling","cp-weights","cp-smoke","cp-proxy","cp-tp2","cp-bench","cp-close","cp-usb4stream","rocm10-probe"],"frontier":[],"diagnoses":[{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/40","diagnosis":"Recorded a diagnosis-unavailable outcome: the steward node for task cp-weights ended without projecting a diagnosis (result-schema-mismatch), so nothing judged this failure and no retry may be dispatched on a judgment nobody made. Failing check id: 'cp-weights'. Node detail: {\"code\":\"result-schema-mismatch\",\"message\":\"node result does not match resultSchema: /proposal: \\\"acceptanceCriteria\\\" is a required property; /proposal: Additional properties are not allowed ('acceptance' was unexpected)\",\"details\":{\"errors\":[\"/proposal: \\\"acceptanceCriteria\\\" is a required property\",\"/proposal: Additional properties are not allowed ('acceptance' was unexpected)\"]}}.","taskId":"cp-weights","verdict":"blocked"},{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/41","diagnosis":"Reproduced the cp-smoke failure in-container and isolated it to a probe defect in scripts/run-smoke.sh rather than in the engine under test. Evidence: I re-ran the checkpoint's in-container python against a scratch /results mount (image localhost/flashnext:dev, the same image cp-build receipted). podman exited 0; four of five probes passed (arch gfx1151/on_cdna=false, fp8_cast e4m3fn_alloc_and_cast=true, registry model_arch_registered=true, aperture ttm_pages_limit=33554432). The fifth failed with `TypeError: cannot unpack non-iterable bool object` at the `ok, why = TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym)` line of the admission() probe. The engine itself admitted correctly on the very same run — stdout carries `INFO [triton_moe.py:177] TritonExperts: admitting block-FP8 fused MoE (...) on gfx1151 via in-kernel bf16 upcast`. The contract mismatch is in the probe: patches/0008 defines `_supports_quant_scheme` as a plain boolean predicate (its own pinned tests assert `assert TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(*BLOCK_FP8_SCHEME)` and `assert not ...` directly), so the two-tuple unpack in the smoke script can never succeed. Consequence chain matches the capture exactly: try_() catches the TypeError, sets status=fail, the receipt lands at results/receipts/failed/smoke.json instead of results/receipts/smoke.json, the trailing verifier finds no passing receipt and exits 1 — which is why the archived capture shows only `smoke receipt: .../results/receipts/smoke.json (fail receipts land under results/receipts/failed/)` with an empty stderr and exit 1. Blocked rather than retry for two independent reasons: cp-smoke is kind=checkpoint with a worklist-fixed argv and a brief that forbids repository modification, so it holds no authority to edit the script; and scripts/run-smoke.sh appears in no task's conflictDomains in silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json (host-tooling owns only scripts/run-tp2.sh, proxy-tooling owns scripts/make-proxy.sh and scripts/run-proxy.sh, usb4stream-bench owns scripts/receipts-verify.py), so no existing lane can land the fix either. A retry of cp-smoke would reproduce the identical TypeError, since HEAD equals baseRev 1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304 and the diff is empty. The fix is a one-line contract correction in the probe plus a deterministic-timestamp change to satisfy checkpoint purity; it needs an amendment task holding scripts/run-smoke.sh.\n\nCheckpoint capture: /home/tom/.local/state/tally/capture/archive/01a05128-426c-7d42-aedc-87c2c63848f1.cp-smoke/checkpoint.json","proposal":{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","bash -n scripts/run-smoke.sh && grep -q '_supports_quant_scheme' scripts/run-smoke.sh && ! grep -Eq '(ok|admitted)[[:space:]]*,[[:space:]]*why[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*TritonExperts\\._supports_quant_scheme' scripts/run-smoke.sh"],"description":"The smoke script no longer unpacks the boolean _supports_quant_scheme hook into a two-tuple, still calls the hook, and remains syntax-clean.","id":"smoke-admission-contract"},{"argv":["bash","scripts/run-smoke.sh"],"description":"The in-container smoke runs to completion and exits 0 against the cp-build image.","id":"smoke-runs-green"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","python3 -c \"import json,os,sys; r=json.load(open('results/receipts/smoke.json')); assert r['status']=='pass', r['status']; assert r['data']['admission']['fp8_block_moe_admitted'] is True, r['data']['admission']; assert not os.path.exists('results/receipts/failed/smoke.json'), 'fail receipt shadows the pass'\""],"description":"A passing receipt exists at results/receipts/smoke.json, records fp8_block_moe_admitted true, and no fail receipt shadows it.","id":"smoke-receipt-pass"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","bash scripts/run-smoke.sh >/dev/null && git diff --quiet -- . && git diff --quiet --cached -- . && test -z \"$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no)\""],"description":"Re-running the smoke over an already-correct base leaves every tracked file byte-identical, per checkpoint purity.","id":"smoke-idempotent-on-tracked-paths"}],"dependencies":["cp-build"],"goal":"Grant a short implementation lane authority over scripts/run-smoke.sh and correct the admission probe so the in-container smoke grades the engine instead of tripping over its own call contract. Required changes: (1) In the admission() probe, stop unpacking the return of TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme as a two-tuple. The fork's hook (patches/0008) is a plain boolean predicate, as its own pinned tests assert. Call it as `admitted = bool(TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym))` when the attribute exists, and keep the existing missing-hook fallback reporting fp8_block_moe_admitted=false with reason 'no hook'. Preserve the receipt's data.admission shape ({\"fp8_block_moe_admitted\": bool, \"reason\": str}) so downstream receipt graders keep working; supply a reason string derived locally (for example 'bool predicate admitted' / 'bool predicate refused') rather than a value returned by the hook. Do not weaken the probe into a pass-by-default: a false predicate must still set status=fail and route the receipt to results/receipts/failed/. (2) Satisfy OVERSEER STANDING NOTE 2 (checkpoint purity) for results/receipts/smoke.json: the receipt's ts must not be a fresh strftime on every run. Before writing, read any existing committed results/receipts/smoke.json; if every measured fact in data is byte-identical to the new measurement, reuse the existing ts and rewrite the file byte-identically (or skip the write) so a re-run over an already-correct base leaves tracked files unchanged and exits 0. Only stamp a new timestamp when a measured fact actually changed. (3) Land the resulting passing receipt at results/receipts/smoke.json in the lane commit, and leave the trailing verifier's failed/-beats-passing precedence logic intact. Do not touch patches/, container/, or any engine source: the engine behaviour is already correct and was observed admitting block-FP8 fused MoE on gfx1151 during reproduction.","kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},"taskId":"cp-smoke","verdict":"blocked"}],"retries":[{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/38","reason":"Stage `checkpoint:record` faulted.\n\n{\"code\":\"result-schema-mismatch\",\"message\":\"adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" child exited 1 (failed); stderr tail: spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base; configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\",\"details\":{\"projection\":{\"code\":\"result-projection-timeout\",\"message\":\"adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" child exited 1 (failed); stderr tail: spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base; configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\",\"details\":{\"adapter\":\"spec-build-driver\",\"attempt\":1,\"taskUuid\":\"01a0511c-5a48-7750-9a19-413830b669e0\",\"timeoutMs\":10000,\"exitEvidencePassed\":false,\"verdict\":\"failed\",\"exitCode\":1,\"stderrTail\":\"spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base\",\"stderrTruncated\":false,\"projectionTimeoutMessage\":\"configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\"}}}}","taskId":"cp-weights"},{"attempt":2,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/39","reason":"Stage `checkpoint:record` faulted.\n\n{\"code\":\"result-schema-mismatch\",\"message\":\"adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" child exited 1 (failed); stderr tail: spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base; configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\",\"details\":{\"projection\":{\"code\":\"result-projection-timeout\",\"message\":\"adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" child exited 1 (failed); stderr tail: spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base; configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\",\"details\":{\"adapter\":\"spec-build-driver\",\"attempt\":1,\"taskUuid\":\"01a0511f-8104-7852-b56e-56103c77c931\",\"timeoutMs\":10000,\"exitEvidencePassed\":false,\"verdict\":\"failed\",\"exitCode\":1,\"stderrTail\":\"spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base\",\"stderrTruncated\":false,\"projectionTimeoutMessage\":\"configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\"}}}}","taskId":"cp-weights"}],"outcomes":[],"deferrals":[],"blocked":[{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling"],"taskId":"proxy-tooling"},{"blockedBy":["cp-weights"],"taskId":"cp-weights"},{"blockedBy":["cp-smoke"],"taskId":"cp-smoke"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling","cp-smoke"],"taskId":"cp-proxy"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling","cp-weights","cp-smoke"],"taskId":"cp-tp2"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling","cp-weights","cp-smoke"],"taskId":"cp-bench"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling","cp-weights","cp-smoke"],"taskId":"cp-close"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling","cp-weights","cp-smoke"],"taskId":"cp-usb4stream"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling","cp-weights","cp-smoke"],"taskId":"rocm10-probe"}],"quiescent":true,"escalation":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/30","closingSummary":null,"warnings":["task proxy-tooling latched for human attention after 10 lifetime attempt receipts (hard limit 10)"]},"maintenance":{"blockingJobs":[],"cleaned":[],"currentRunHash":"a9309e9870ae","liveRuns":[],"warnings":[]},"checkpoints":[],"merged":[],"published":{"action":"already-published","baseBranch":"main","integrationHead":"1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304","provenHead":"1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304","reason":"the gate-proven head 1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304 is already reachable from main","receipt":{"actor":"spec-build-driver","baseBranch":"main","campaign":"flashnext","provenBy":{"reference":"refs/tally/spec-build/v1/9580b7cc868de0369023d414/checkpoint/cp-build-d82210748f7034f64b1b43cd6bc45335a56b8449998229249233645d6a8b243d/1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304","taskId":"cp-build"},"schemaVersion":1,"sha":"1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304","writtenAt":"2026-08-30T05:55:16.141Z"},"receiptRef":"refs/tally/spec-build/v1/9580b7cc868de0369023d414/publish/1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304","regateRequired":false,"sha":"1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304"},"failures":[],"diagnoses":[],"retries":[],"outcomes":[],"deferrals":[],"continuation":null,"escalation":null}}}
